# Testing Conventions

## Framework

- Vitest with ESM support
- Test files mirror `src/` structure under `test/` (e.g., `test/services/thumbnail.test.ts`)
- Alternatively, co-locate as `*.test.ts` next to source files

## Patterns

- Use `describe`/`it` blocks with descriptive names
- Prefer `expect` assertions over manual checks
- Use `beforeEach`/`afterEach` for setup and teardown
- Use `vi.mock()` for module mocking, `vi.fn()` for function stubs
- Mock `child_process.execFile` for FFmpeg tests (don't require FFmpeg in CI)
- Use in-memory SQLite for database tests (`:memory:`)

## What to Test

- Service logic: input → output, edge cases, error conditions
- Route handlers: request/response shape, auth enforcement, status codes
- Utility functions: pure functions with known inputs/outputs
- Security filter: per-model access control rules

## What Not to Test

- Drizzle schema definitions (tested implicitly by migrations)
- sharp/onnxruntime internals (trust the library, test your wrapper)
- Fastify framework behavior (test your handlers, not the framework)

## Running Tests

- `pnpm test` — run all tests once
- `pnpm vitest run path/to/test.ts` — run a single test file
- `pnpm test:watch` — watch mode for development
